title: 'Zombienet: Reduce flakyness of AD full-mesh test'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    I was looking a bit into recent merge-queue failures. And this AD test was at the flaky top.

    **Problems and fixes:**
    - Sequential key updates could cross session boundaries, and readiness accepted partial activation -> Batch all six updates atomically and wait for the exact new key set on every collator.
    - Discovery readiness counted addresses instead of peers -> Count distinct peer IDs.
    - Ordinary peer counts included full nodes. Require all five collator peers to resolve and verify the full mesh.
crates:
- name: cumulus-client-collator-discovery
  bump: patch
